{"version":1,"slug":"organized__Others__General_Awareness__General_Studies__Super_Practice__SSC_CGL_MOCKS_2025_SSC_SUPER_PRACTICE_41858","path":"organized/Others/General Awareness/General Studies/Super Practice/@SSC_CGL_MOCKS_2025_SSC SUPER PRACTICE_41858.html","title":"devgagan","provider":"organized","category":"Others/General Awareness/General Studies/Super Practice","durationMinutes":60,"totalQuestions":20,"sectionsLocked":false,"sections":null,"questions":[{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>A wheel makes 700 revolutions to cover a distance of 77 kilometres. What will be the diameter of the wheel?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2346;&#2361;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; 77 &#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379;&#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2370;&#2352;&#2368; &#2340;&#2351; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; 700 &#2330;&#2325;&#2381;&#2325;&#2352; &#2354;&#2327;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2346;&#2361;&#2367;&#2351;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2360; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2366;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">25 m</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">25 &#2350;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">30 m</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">30 &#2350;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">20 m</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">20 &#2350;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">35 m</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">35 &#2350;&#2368;</span>"],"correct_option_id":3,"solution":"<p>Distance covered by wheel in 1 revolution = &#960;*diameter</p><p>Therefore distance covered in 700 revolutions = 700* &#960;*diameter</p><p>According to question, 700* &#960;*diameter = 77*1000</p><p>Diameter = 77*1000*7/(22*700) = 35 m</p><p>Hence, the diameter of wheel is 35 m.</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>The perimeter of a triangle is 30 cm and its area is numerically equal to the sum of its sides. If one of the sides measures 12 cm, what is the length (in cm) of the largest side of the triangle?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346; 30 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2311;&#2360;&#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2350;&#2325; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2360;&#2375; &#2311;&#2360;&#2325;&#2368; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2351;&#2379;&#2327; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2352;&#2366;&#2348;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2319;&#2325; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368; &#2350;&#2366;&#2346; 12 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2348;&#2360;&#2375; &#2348;&#2337;&#2364;&#2368; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; (&#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">12 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">12 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">13 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">13 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">14 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">14 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">15 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">15 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p>Let the largest side of the triangle be x cm.</p><p>Given, one of the sides = 12 cm.</p><p>&#8756; The remaining two sides are x cm and (18 - x) cm.</p><p>Given, area of the triangle = perimeter</p><p>=&gt; &radic;{15(15 - 12)(15 - x)(15 - 18 + x)} = 30 [According to Heron's formula]</p><p>=&gt; 15 * 3 * (15 - x) (x - 3) = 30 * 30</p><p>=&gt; (15 - x)(x - 3) = 20</p><p>=&gt; 15x - 45 - x&#178; + 3x = 20</p><p>=&gt; x&#178; - 18x + 65 = 0</p><p>=&gt; (x - 13)(x - 5) = 0</p><p>=&gt; x = 13 cm (largest side of the triangle).</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>If area of circle is halved when its radius is decreased by n then what will be the radius of the circle?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; n &#2328;&#2335;&#2366;&#2344;&#2375; &#2346;&#2352; &#2313;&#2360;&#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; &#2310;&#2343;&#2366; &#2361;&#2379; &#2332;&#2366;&#2319; &#2340;&#2379; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2368;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">n/(&radic;2-1)</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">n/(&radic;2-1)</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">2n/(&radic;2-2)</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">2n/(&radic;2-2)</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">&radic;(2n)/&radic;2-2</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&radic;(2n)/&radic;2-2</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">&radic;2n/(&radic;2-1)</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&radic;2n/(&radic;2-1)</span>"],"correct_option_id":3,"solution":"<p>Let us suppose radius of the circle be R.</p><p>Hence according to the question, (pR<sup>2</sup>/p(R-n)<sup>2</sup>) = 2/1</p><p>=&gt; R<sup>2</sup>/(R-n)<sup>2</sup> = 2/1</p><p>=&gt; &radic;2 (R-n) = R</p><p>=&gt; &radic;2R  -  R = &radic;2n</p><p>=&gt; R(&radic;2-1) = &radic;2n</p><p>=&gt; R = &radic;2n/(&radic;2-1)</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>The area of a circular paper is p cm<sup>2</sup>. The area of an equilateral triangle is q cm<sup>2</sup>. If the side of the triangle is half the radius of the circle, then which of the following relations between p and q is correct?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2366;&#2327;&#2332;&#2364; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; p &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>2</sup> &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2350;&#2348;&#2366;&#2361;&#2369; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; q &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>2</sup> &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2368; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368; &#2310;&#2343;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; p &#2324;&#2352; q &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; &#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344; &#2360;&#2366; &#2360;&#2306;&#2348;&#2306;&#2343; &#2360;&#2361;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">&radic;3p = 4&#960;q</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&radic;3p = 4&#960;q</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">4p = &radic;3&#960;q</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">4p = &radic;3&#960;q</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">&radic;3p = 16&#960;q</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&radic;3p = 16&#960;q</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">3&#960;p = 16q</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">3&#960;p = 16q</span>"],"correct_option_id":2,"solution":"<p>r = 2a</p><p>p = &#960;r<sup>2 </sup>= &#960;(2a)<sup>2 </sup>= 4a<sup>2</sup>&#960;</p><p>q = (&radic;3/4) * a<sup>2</sup></p><p>So, p/q = 4a<sup>2</sup>&#960;/(&radic;3/4)a<sup>2</sup></p><p>p/q = 16&#960;/&radic;3</p><p>&radic;3p = 16&#960;q</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>From a circular sheet of area 1386 cm<sup>2</sup>, 2 cm wide five circular rings of variable radius were cut. What percentage of the sheet remained?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>1386 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;2 &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2368; 2 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2330;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364;&#2368; &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2358;&#2368;&#2335; &#2360;&#2375; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368;&#2351; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2366;&#2306;&#2330; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2331;&#2354;&#2381;&#2354;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366;&#2335;&#2375; &#2327;&#2319;&#2404; &#2358;&#2368;&#2335; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; &#2349;&#2366;&#2327; &#2358;&#2375;&#2359; &#2348;&#2330;&#2366;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">21.2%</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">21.2%</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">23.8%</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">23.8%</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">25.7%</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">25.7%</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">27.4%</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">27.4%</span>"],"correct_option_id":3,"solution":"<p>As we know, area of circle = &#960;r<sup>2</sup>, where 'r' is the radius of the circle</p><p>=&gt; Radius of sheet = &radic;[(1386  X  7)/22] = &radic;441 = 21 cm</p><p>&#8757; 5 rings of 2 cm width is cut,</p><p>=&gt; Radius of remaining sheet = 21  -  5(2) = 11 cm</p><p>Area of remaining sheet = (22/7)  X  11  X  11 = 380.3 cm<sup>2</sup></p><p>&#8756; Percentage of remaining sheet = (380.3/1386)  X  100 = 27.4%</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>The perimeter of an equilateral triangle is 144 cm. Find the area of the triangle. </p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2350;&#2348;&#2366;&#2361;&#2369; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346; 144 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">784&radic;3 cm<sup>2</sup></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">784&radic;3 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>2</sup></span>","<span class=\"eqt\">576&radic;3 cm<sup>2</sup></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">576&radic;3 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>2</sup></span>","<span class=\"eqt\">584&radic;3 cm<sup>2</sup></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">584&radic;3 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>2</sup></span>","<span class=\"eqt\">676&radic;3 cm<sup>2</sup></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">676&radic;3 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>2</sup></span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p>The side of the triangle = 144/3 = 48 cm</p><p>The area of an equilateral triangle = &radic;3/4 * (side)<sup>2</sup></p><p>= &radic;3/4 * (48 * 48) </p><p>= 576&radic;3 cm<sup>2</sup></p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Find the area of a right-angle triangle whose hypotenuse is 89 cm and base is 39 cm.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2350;&#2325;&#2379;&#2339; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319; &#2332;&#2367;&#2360;&#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339; 89 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2324;&#2352; &#2310;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352; 39 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">1735.5 cm<sup>2</sup></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">1735.5 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>2</sup></span>","<span class=\"eqt\"><sup> </sup>1644.5 cm<sup>2</sup></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><sup> </sup>1644.5 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>2</sup></span>","<span class=\"eqt\"><sup> </sup>1560 cm<sup>2</sup></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><sup> </sup>1560 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>2</sup></span>","<span class=\"eqt\"><sup> </sup>1480 cm<sup>2</sup></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><sup> </sup>1480 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>2</sup></span>"],"correct_option_id":2,"solution":"<p>Height = &radic;(Hypotenuse<sup>2</sup>  -  Base<sup>2</sup>) </p><p>= &radic;(89<sup>2</sup>  -  39<sup>2</sup>)</p><p>= 80 cm </p><p>Area of right triangle = 1/2 * Base * Height </p><p>= 1/2 * 80 * 39 </p><p>= 1560 cm<sup>2</sup></p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>If three sides of the triangle are given as 53 cm, 56 cm, and 53 cm, then find the area of the triangle. </p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2368;&#2344; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366;&#2319;&#2305; 53 cm, 56 cm &#2324;&#2352; 53 cm &#2342;&#2368; &#2327;&#2312; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">1236 cm<sup>2</sup></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">1236 cm<sup>2</sup></span>","<span class=\"eqt\">1248 cm<sup>2</sup></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">1248 cm<sup>2</sup></span>","<span class=\"eqt\">1244 cm<sup>2</sup></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">1244 cm<sup>2</sup></span>","<span class=\"eqt\">1260 cm<sup>2</sup></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">1260 cm<sup>2</sup></span>"],"correct_option_id":3,"solution":"<p><img width=180 height=150 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p24306/image001.png\" ></p><p>In right angle triangle,</p><p>AD<sup>2</sup> + DC<sup>2</sup> = AC<sup>2</sup></p><p>AD<sup>2</sup> + 28<sup>2</sup> = 53<sup>2</sup></p><p>AD<sup>2</sup> = 2809  -  784 </p><p>AD = 45</p><p>Area of triangle ABC = 1/2 * base * height </p><p>= 1/2 * 56 * 45 </p><p>= 1260 cm<sup>2</sup> </p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Two sides of a triangular field are 25 meters and 17 meters respectively and its perimeter is 54 meters. Find the area of the field.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2350;&#2376;&#2342;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2379; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366;&#2319;&#2306; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 25 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2324;&#2352; 17 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2313;&#2360;&#2325;&#2368; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346; 54 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376; | &#2340;&#2379; &#2350;&#2376;&#2342;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">85sqm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">85 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">75sqm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">75 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">100sqm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">100 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">90sqm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">90 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;</span>"],"correct_option_id":3,"solution":"<p>Perimeter =sum of 3 sides of the field.</p> <p>So third side of the triangle field= 54-(25+17) =12 meter</p> <p>S =(25+17+12)/2=27</p> <p>Area of the triangle field =square root of (27*(27-25)*(27-17)(27-12))</p> <p>Area = square root of (27*2*10*15)</p> <p>Hence Area of the triangle field =90 square meter</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>The side of an equilateral triangle whose area is 25&radic;3 cm<sup>2</sup> is-</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>______ &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2350;&#2348;&#2366;&#2361;&#2369; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; 25&radic;3 cm<sup>2</sup> &#2361;&#2376;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">50cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">50cm</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">40cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">40cm</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">10cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">10cm</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">20cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">20cm</span>"],"correct_option_id":2,"solution":"<p>Area of an equilateral triangle is given by the formula</p><p>Area = (&radic;3/4) a*a = 25(&radic;3)</p><p>Side = 10 cm</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>The radius of a circular land is 84 m. If the cost of fencing the circumference of the land with bamboo sticks is Rs. 25 per meter, then what is the total cost of fencing the land with bamboo sticks?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2349;&#2370;&#2350;&#2367; &#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; 84 m &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2349;&#2370;&#2350;&#2367; &#2325;&#2368; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2343;&#2367; &#2325;&#2379; &#2348;&#2366;&#2306;&#2360; &#2325;&#2368; &#2337;&#2306;&#2337;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2348;&#2366;&#2337;&#2364; &#2354;&#2327;&#2366;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2366;&#2327;&#2340; &#2352;&#2369;. 25 &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; (m) &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2348;&#2366;&#2306;&#2360; &#2325;&#2368; &#2337;&#2306;&#2337;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2349;&#2370;&#2350;&#2367; &#2325;&#2368; &#2348;&#2366;&#2337;&#2364; &#2354;&#2327;&#2366;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2354;&#2366;&#2327;&#2340; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">Rs. 14400</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2352;&#2369;. 14400</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Rs. 13200</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2352;&#2369;. 13200</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Rs. 15600</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2352;&#2369;. 15600</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Rs. 12800</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2352;&#2369;. 12800</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p>The radius of a circular land is 84 m.</p><p>If the cost of fencing the circumference of the land with bamboo sticks is Rs. 25 per meter.</p><p>So, total cost = 2 * 22/7 * 84 * 25 = Rs. 13200</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>The area of a circular field is 9856 cm<sup>2</sup>. If a person crosses the field along the diameter, calculate the distance that he will travel (in cm).</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2349;&#2370;&#2350;&#2367; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; 9856 cm<sup>2 </sup>&#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340;&#2367; &#2313;&#2360; &#2349;&#2370;&#2350;&#2367; &#2325;&#2379; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2360; &#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2366;&#2341; &#2346;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2313;&#2360;&#2325;&#2375; &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2340;&#2351; &#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2312; &#2342;&#2370;&#2352;&#2368; (cm &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2339;&#2344;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">56</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">56</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">112</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">112</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">168</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">168</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">28</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">28</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p>&#960;r<sup>2</sup> = 9856</p><p>=&gt; (22/7) r<sup>2</sup>=9856</p><p>=&gt; r<sup>2</sup>=9856*7/22</p><p>=&gt; r= 56</p><p>So, the distance that he has to travel = 2*56 = 112 cm</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Perimeter of an equilateral triangle is 36 cm and perimeter of circle is 220 cm. Find the difference between side of triangle and radius of circle. (use &#960; = 22/7)</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2350;&#2348;&#2366;&#2361;&#2369; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346; 36 cm &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2343;&#2367; 220 cm &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2368; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366; &#2324;&#2352; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404; (&#960; = 22/7 &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2351;&#2379;&#2327; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306;)</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">21 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">21 cm</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">23 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">23 cm</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">25 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">25 cm</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">27 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">27 cm</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p>Perimeter of equilateral triangle</p><p>Side of triangle = 36/3 = 12 cm</p><p>Perimeter of circle = 2 &#960;r</p><p>According to question,</p><p>2 &#960;r = 220</p><p>2 * 22/7 * r = 220</p><p>r = 220 * 7/(22 * 2)</p><p>r = 35 cm</p><p>Required difference = 35  -  12 = 23 cm</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>If the perimeter of an equilateral triangle is 108&radic;3 cm. Find the height of triangle.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2350;&#2348;&#2366;&#2361;&#2369; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346; 108&radic;3 cm &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2368; &#2314;&#2305;&#2330;&#2366;&#2312; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">27cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">27cm</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">54cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">54cm</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">81cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">81cm</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">108cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">108cm</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p>Let the side of equilateral triangle be a.</p><p>Perimeter of equilateral triangle = 3a.</p><p>Given perimeter = 108&radic;3</p><p>Therefore side = 36&radic;3.</p><p>Height of equilateral triangle = (&radic;3/2) * a= 54cm</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>The cost of building a fence around a circular field is Rs 7425 at the rate of Rs 13.5 per foot. What is the area of the circular field?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2350;&#2376;&#2342;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2375; &#2330;&#2366;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2323;&#2352; &#2348;&#2366;&#2337;&#2364; &#2348;&#2344;&#2366;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2366;&#2327;&#2340; 13.5 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2347;&#2369;&#2335; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2352; &#2360;&#2375; 7425 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2350;&#2376;&#2342;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">24062.5 sq.ft</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">24062.5 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2347;&#2369;&#2335;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">23864.4 sq.ft.</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">23864.4 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2347;&#2369;&#2335;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">24644.5 sq.ft.</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">24644.5 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2347;&#2369;&#2335;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">25018.5 sq.ft</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">25018.5 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2347;&#2369;&#2335;</span>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p>Circumference of the plot = 7425/13.5 = 550 feet.</p> <p>2 x 22/7 x R = 550</p> <p>=&gt; R = 550 x 7/22x2 = 87.5 feet</p> <p>Area = 22/7 x 87.5 x 87.5 = 24062.5 sq.ft</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Maximum value of circumference of a circle inscribed in a square is 176 cm. What is the difference between area of circle and area of square? (take &#960; = 22/7)</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327;&#2340; &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2343;&#2367; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325;&#2340;&#2350; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; 176 cm &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2375; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; &#2324;&#2352; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2325;&#2375; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;? (&#960; = 22/7 &#2354;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;)</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">564 cm<sup>2</sup></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">564 cm<sup>2</sup></span>","<span class=\"eqt\">498 cm<sup>2</sup></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">498 cm<sup>2</sup></span>","<span class=\"eqt\">672 cm<sup>2</sup></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">672 cm<sup>2</sup></span>","<span class=\"eqt\">716 cm<sup>2</sup></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">716 cm<sup>2</sup></span>"],"correct_option_id":2,"solution":"<p>Circumference of circle = 2 * (22/7) * radius = 176</p><p>Radius = 28 cm</p><p>Then, side of square = 2 * 28 = 56 cm</p><p>Then, area of square = 56 * 56 = 3136</p><p>Area of circle = (22/7) * 28 * 28 = 2464</p><p>Therefore, difference = 3136  -  2464 = <b>672 cm<sup>2</sup></b></p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>A person started running around a circular track of radius 21 meters with speed of 39.6 km/h. Find the time taken to finish one complete round of the track.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340;&#2367; &#2344;&#2375; 21 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2335;&#2381;&#2352;&#2376;&#2325; &#2325;&#2375; &#2311;&#2352;&#2381;&#2342;-&#2327;&#2367;&#2352;&#2381;&#2342; 39.6 km/h &#2325;&#2368; &#2330;&#2366;&#2354; &#2360;&#2375; &#2342;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364;&#2344;&#2366; &#2310;&#2352;&#2306;&#2349; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;&#2404; &#2335;&#2381;&#2352;&#2376;&#2325; &#2325;&#2366; &#2319;&#2325; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2366; &#2330;&#2325;&#2381;&#2325;&#2352; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2354;&#2327;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2366; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">8 sec</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">8 &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">16 sec</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">16 &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">10 sec</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">10 &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">12 sec</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">12 &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337;</span>"],"correct_option_id":3,"solution":"<p>Total running length = 2&#960;r = 2 * (22/7) * 21</p><p>Speed = 39.6 km/h = 39.6 * (5/18) = 11 m/sec</p><p>Time taken to finish one complete round of the track = 2 * (22/7) * 21 &div; 11</p><p>= 12 sec</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>If radius(R) of one circle is reduced to one fourth and radius(R) of another circle is increased to twice, then sum of the circumference of both the new circles will be_____.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; (R) &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 1/4 &#2349;&#2366;&#2327; &#2340;&#2325; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2350;&#2368; &#2325;&#2368; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2342;&#2370;&#2360;&#2352;&#2375; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; (R) &#2325;&#2379; &#2342;&#2379;&#2327;&#2369;&#2344;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352; &#2342;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2342;&#2379;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2344;&#2319; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2343;&#2367; &#2325;&#2366; &#2351;&#2379;&#2327;&#2347;&#2354; ____ &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2366;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">9&#960;R/2</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">9&#960;R/2</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">4&#960;R/2</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">4&#960;R/2</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">&#960;R/2</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#960;R/2</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">3&#960;R/2</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">3&#960;R/2</span>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p>According to the question,</p><p>Let the original radius be R</p><p>Circumference of the circle = 2&#960;R</p><p>When radius of circle is reduced to &#188;, then Circumference of the circle = 2&#960; (R/4) = &#960;R/2</p><p>When radius of circle is increased twice, then Circumference of the circle = 2&#960; (2R) = 4&#960;R</p><p>Sum of the circumferences = &#960;R/2+ 4&#960;R = 9&#960;R/2</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Find the area of triangle with sides 12 cm, 10 cm and 6 cm.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>12 cm, 10 cm &#2324;&#2352; 6 cm &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">10&radic;14 cm<sup>2</sup></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">10&radic;14 cm<sup>2</sup></span>","<span class=\"eqt\">8&radic;15 cm<sup>2</sup></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">8&radic;15 cm<sup>2</sup></span>","<span class=\"eqt\">9&radic;15 cm<sup>2</sup></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">9&radic;15 cm<sup>2</sup></span>","<span class=\"eqt\">8&radic;14 cm<sup>2</sup></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">8&radic;14 cm<sup>2</sup></span>"],"correct_option_id":3,"solution":"<p>Area of triangle = &radic;s(s-a)(s-b)(s-c)</p><p>Where s = (a + b + c)/2</p><p>According to question,</p><p>s = (12 + 10 + 6)/2 = 14 cm</p><p>Area = &radic;(14 (14  -  12) (14  -  10)(14  -  6))</p><p>= &radic;(14 * 2 * 4 * 8) = &radic;896</p><p>= 8&radic;14 cm<sup>2</sup></p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>What is the area (in cm<sup>2</sup>) of the triangle having sides in the ratio 3: 2: 4 respectively and perimeter 36 cm?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2313;&#2360; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; (cm<sup>2</sup> &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2332;&#2367;&#2360;&#2325;&#2368; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366;&#2319;&#2305; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 3: 2: 4 &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306; &#2324;&#2352; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346; 36 cm &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">10&radic;15</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">10&radic;15</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">12&radic;15</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">12&radic;15</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">14&radic;42</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">14&radic;42</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">16&radic;15</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">16&radic;15</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p>Perimeter = 36 cm</p><p>Then, first side = 36 * 3/9 = 12 cm</p><p>Second side = 36 * 2/9 = 8 cm</p><p>Third side = 36 * 4/9 = 16 cm</p><p>Perimeter/2 = 36/2 = 18 cm</p><p>Therefore, area = &radic;(18 * (18  -  12) * (18  -  8) * (18  -  16))</p><p>= <b>12&radic;15 cm<sup>2</sup></b></p>","marks":2,"section":null}]}